<Layout title="Pediatrician for a college student at Virginia Tech | For parents" description="A Blacksburg pediatrician for the year your student is at Virginia Tech. Refills, ADHD and other ongoing medications, sick visits, forms, and a clear agreement about who we tell.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">For parents</div><h1>A local doctor for the year they're at Virginia Tech.</h1><p class="lead">Refills, ADHD and other ongoing medications, sick days, university forms, and a clear agreement about who we tell. Schiffert Health Center is the campus clinic they will also use. We hold the year-long plan.</p></div>
<div class="w"><img class="photo" src={href("photos/arch-fall.jpg")} width="678" height="452" alt="A stone arch on campus under fall trees">
<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:40px">Before move-in</div>
<h2>Five things to arrange before they leave home.</h2>
<p class="lead">From the AAP college-health checklist and Virginia Tech's own forms.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Establish care in Blacksburg</h3><p>Know who their doctor is in town before the first sick day. We meet them for a baseline visit and take the plan the hometown doctor already has.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Transfer ADHD and other mental-health prescriptions</h3><p>Campus clinics often refer ADHD medication to a community doctor. Anxiety and depression medications that started at home need a local prescriber too. Set that up before move-in.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Complete the immunization form</h3><p>Virginia Tech requires an Immunization History Form, signed by a healthcare provider, in the Healthy Hokies portal.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="num">4</div><h3>SSD housing letter, if they need one</h3><p>Housing accommodations go through Services for Students with Disabilities and need health-provider documentation. Air conditioning, a single room, and similar requests start with that letter.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="num">5</div><h3>Decide who we may update</h3><p>At 18 the chart is theirs. Before care begins, we write down what they want shared with you and with the hometown doctor — and we follow it.</p></div>
</div>
<p class="cite"><a href="https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/young-adult/Pages/Healthy-Tips-for-the-College-Freshman.aspx">AAP / HealthyChildren college checklist</a>. <a href="https://healthcenter.vt.edu/new_student/required_immunizations.html">VT required immunizations</a>. <a href="https://ssd.vt.edu/access/housing.html">VT SSD housing access</a>.</p>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">What we hold while they're here</div>
<h2>The work, week to week.</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Refills and ongoing medications</h3><p>ADHD, anxiety, depression, asthma, thyroid, and the rest of the plan they already have. We keep it active and copy the hometown doctor when something changes.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Sick days</h3><p>A doctor in town who already knows their baseline. Usually same week, and often same day.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>University forms</h3><p>Housing and SSD letters, immunizations, club and athletic physicals, travel health paperwork.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Who we tell</h3><p>The standing rule you agree on together. Their hometown doctor gets a clinical update the same day when something shifts.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">Why parents look for this</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>The plan they already have</h3><p>Forty-four percent of college students report at least one listed mental-health diagnosis. These conditions do not disappear in college. Away from home, they often get more complicated.</p><p class="cite">ACHA-NCHA III, Fall 2024 reference group, 33,763 students at 48 U.S. institutions. <a href="https://www.acha.org/wp-content/uploads/NCHA-IIIb_FALL_2024_REFERENCE_GROUP_EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.pdf">Executive summary (PDF)</a>.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Care away from home</h3><p>Schiffert is useful for many visits and is already in the student health fee. A year-long plan — especially ongoing prescriptions campus clinics often send out — needs a doctor who already knows them.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>The expensive default</h3><p>An ER visit can cost hundreds of dollars—or several thousand on a high-deductible plan or limited student insurance. If it is a true emergency, call 911. Otherwise, start with a doctor who already knows them.</p><p class="cite">Large-employer plans averaged $646 out of pocket. <a href="https://www.kff.org/health-costs/emergency-department-visits-exceed-affordability-threshold-for-many-consumers-with-private-insurance/">KFF / Peterson-Kaiser Health System Tracker</a>, 2019 claims (published 2022).</p></div>
</div>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">The four things we hold</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Continuous chronic care</h3><p>Your established treatment plan stays active and monitored. We manage ongoing care locally and keep their hometown doctor fully updated when anything shifts.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Building adult health habits</h3><p>College is where young adults take ownership of their health. We guide them through navigating appointments, refills, and self-care so they are prepared for independence.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Collaborative communication</h3><p>Respecting your student's adult privacy while keeping you informed. We establish clear communication boundaries together, and their hometown doctor receives a clinical update the same day.</p></div></div></div>
<section><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Nearby, in practice</div><h2>A partner in Blacksburg.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg><h3>Direct physician access</h3><p>A direct line to their doctor in Blacksburg. No call center and no nurse triage tree.</p></div><div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg><h3>Seen in town</h3><p>The panel stays small so they can usually be seen the same week, and often the same day.</p></div><div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-compass"/></svg><h3>Hometown coordination</h3><p>Their hometown pediatrician is designated on day one, copied on clinical notes, and sent a year-end summary every May.</p></div></div>
<div style="text-align:center;margin-top:48px"><h2>A local partner for the year they're here.</h2><p class="lead" style="margin:16px auto 28px">A board-certified pediatrician in Blacksburg who treats what they actually need, and stays in step with the doctor at home.</p>
<p><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a> &nbsp; <a class="lnk" href={href("membership")}>Membership &rarr;</a></p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
